l", "source": "NBC Boston", "published": "2026-09-10T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}, {"title": "Governor’s race set between Healey and Minogue", "source": "WHDH", "published": "2026-09-02T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE9iejFHZnZtQXZ4bW4wSDB1LTduVDNTUl9EbkhheWw2SXViYVdLNk43WFh1MmZnXzJBWlpIaHNOOTNkOVF0VzdPTF9ObkQzTjlIY0czQUV4RlcxY05NdkNFUVpiWVhtYUxKR2FZR0RNckY0cTdoNUpz?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 17.04, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 19.68, "poll_sd": 5.88, "poll_weight": 0.45, "fundamentals": {"margin": 18.6, "lean": 10.5, "environment": 4.1, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.4, "baseline_margin": 18.23, "analyst_adjustment": -0.23, "key_factors": ["Healey has led by 16-24 points in every poll this cycle, including 16-21 in the latest September surveys", "All seven expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column", "Kalshi and Polymarket both price Healey's win probability near 96 percent", "Minogue's record $6.1 million self-spending has narrowed but not fundamentally changed the race"], "rationale": "Independent pollsters consistently show Healey ahead by double digits in a D+14 state, raters unanimously call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and markets price her near 96 percent. Minogue's heavy self-funding has trimmed a few points off the lead without altering the fundamentals.", "watch": "A sustained fall advertising push from Minogue's personal fortune could narrow the margin further, as the most recent surveys already show some tightening.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Maura Healey seeks a second term against Republican nominee Mike Minogue, a self-funded businessman, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. The state leans heavily Democratic, and all seven major race ratings place the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column. Polling has been stable all year, with Healey leading by 16 to 24 points in surveys from UNH, MassINC, UMass Amherst and Suffolk.\n\nPrediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket put Healey's chances near 96 percent. Minogue spent a record $6.1 million in a single month and campaigns on affordability and auditing Beacon Hill, drawing criticism from union leaders about his wealth. Boston Mayor Wu has endorsed Healey, and surveys find Trump prominent in voters' minds, a dynamic that has worked in the incumbent's favor. The open question is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}]}